{
  "id": "21442_musou",
  "headword": "{夢想|むそう}",
  "reading": "むそう",
  "romaji": "musou",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "daydream; fantasy; reverie",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "daydream, fantasy, reverie, idle fancy",
      "explanation": "Indulging in pleasant but unrealistic thoughts or imaginings. Often implies that the thoughts are detached from reality or unlikely to be realized."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21442_musou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{将来|しょうらい}のことを{夢想|むそう}する。",
      "english": "To daydream about the future.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21442_musou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{窓|まど}の{外|そと}を{眺|なが}めながら{夢想|むそう}にふけっていた。",
      "english": "He was lost in reverie, gazing out the window.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21442_musou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{世界|せかい}{平和|へいわ}なんて{夢想|むそう}にすぎないと{言|い}う{人|ひと}もいるが、{理想|りそう}を{持|も}つことは{大切|たいせつ}だ。",
      "english": "Some say world peace is nothing but a fantasy, but it is important to have ideals.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {夢|む} (dream) and {想|そう} (thought, imagination). The verb form is {夢想|むそう}する. Has a literary tone and often carries a nuance of unrealistic thinking, though it can also be used more neutrally for imaginative contemplation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {夢想|むそう}にふける: to be lost in daydreams\n- {夢想|むそう}{家|か}: a dreamer, a visionary\n- {夢想|むそう}にすぎない: to be nothing but a fantasy\n- {夢想|むそう}する: to daydream, to fantasize\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {空想|くうそう}: fantasy, daydream — very similar but slightly more neutral; also used in {空想|くうそう}{科学|かがく}{小説|しょうせつ} (science fiction)\n- {妄想|もうそう}: delusion, paranoid fantasy — stronger negative nuance, implies irrational or obsessive thinking\n- {幻想|げんそう}: illusion, fantasy — emphasizes something illusory or enchanting",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
